        "original_id": "8dd5a0e9-c26e-5228-be84-7de4b1ffdcc6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Misadventures of Merlin Jones, In Search of the Castaways, The Monkey's Uncle, Moving Day\n- People: Tommy Kirk, Annette Funicello, Hayley Mills, Maurice Chevalier, Robert Stevenson, Lowell S. Hawley, Jules Verne, Ben Sharpsteen, Walt Disney, Clarence Nash, Pinto Colvig, Billy Bletcher\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, Walt Disney production\n- Roles: director, screenplay writer, voice cast\n- Works: Captain Grant's Children\n\nFacts:\n- Jules Verne wrote the 1868 adventure novel \"Captain Grant's Children.\"\n- Moving Day is a 1936 film directed by Ben Sharpsteen.\n- Walt Disney voiced Mickey, Clarence Nash voiced Donald, Pinto Colvig voiced Goofy, and Billy Bletcher voiced Pete as the Sheriff in Moving Day.\n- In Search of the Castaways is a 1962 Walt Disney Productions feature film starring Hayley Mills and Maurice Chevalier about a worldwide search for a shipwrecked sea captain.\n- Robert Stevenson directed In Search of the Castaways from a screenplay by Lowell S. Hawley based on Jules Verne's \"Captain Grant's Children.\"\n- The Misadventures of Merlin Jones is a 1964 Walt Disney production starring Tommy Kirk and Annette Funicello.\n- The Monkey's Uncle is a sequel to the 1964 film The Misadventures of Merlin Jones.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
